# vit_v1_endpoint: ViT-Base/16 with s8_encrypt_chunk's seven levers and driver, unchanged.
#
# port       ViTLayer has no attention mask (mask tensor, its encryption and wrapper argument removed);
#            no pooler (final LayerNorm + CLS slice); one pixel_values operand; local checkpoint directory.
# levers     byte-identical to s8_encrypt_chunk, including encrypt_chunk_cpu before encrypt_spill_cpu.
#            Not re-derived (transfer check).
# may not transfer:
#   SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16   chunks a 28,996 x 768 vocabulary table; ViT's embedding (Conv2d over
#                           3 x 224 x 224 plus 197 x 768 positions) is two orders smaller.
#   SHAFT_ENC_CHUNKS=8      threshold 5,000,000 elements; ViT-Base's largest is 768 x 3072 = 2.36M, so
#                           possibly nothing chunked (LEVER|encrypt_chunk_cpu|chunked_params= reports it).
SHAFT_SCRIPT=$BASE/vit_perlayer_stream_cpu.py
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_chunk_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_MODEL=/vit SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16 SHAFT_ENC_CHUNKS=8"
